  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Banwarilal Sharma vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 20 March, 2020 Equivalent citations: Aironline 2020 Mp 580",
    "facts": "This is first application under section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure. The applicant apprehends his arrest in connection with Crime No.382/2019 registered at Police Station- Ambah, District- Morena for the offences punishable under Sections 420, 272, 273 and 120- B of IPC and Sections 51 and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Allegations against the applicant, in short, are that applicant along with co-accused was found involved in manufacturing food unsafe for human consumption at Milk Chiller Center of the co- accused, wherefrom two tankers containing 12000 litres of milk and a loading vehicle carrying 2 15 sacks of Exetrin powder were seized. Learned counsel for the applicant submits that applicant has been falsely implicated. He is neither the owner of the Tankers nor of the business. The offences are triable by JMFC. Except section 420 of the IPC and 51 and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, the rest are bailable in nature. There is no allegation of cheating against the applicant. Nothing has been seized from the applicant.",
    "arguments": "There is no likelihood of his absconsion or tampering with the evidence. Learned Public Prosecutor for the State opposed the HIGH COURT OF MADHYA PRADESH (Banwarilal Sharma Vs. State of M.P.) application and prayed for its rejection by contending that on the basis of the allegations and the material available on record, no case for grant of anticipatory bail is made out. It is also submitted by the learned counsel for the respondent/State that the investigation is pending and custodial interrogation may be required in the matter.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "There is no likelihood of his absconsion or tampering with the evidence. Learned Public Prosecutor for the State opposed the HIGH COURT OF MADHYA PRADESH (Banwarilal Sharma Vs. State of M.P.) application and prayed for its rejection by contending that on the basis of the allegations and the material available on record, no case for grant of anticipatory bail is made out. It is also submitted by the learned counsel for the respondent/State that the investigation is pending and custodial interrogation may be required in the matter.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
